---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import TypedTextDemo from "../../components/TypedTextDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Typed Text"
  description="Text that types itself in when an agent changes it, such as a chat title."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Typed Text</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Types new text in, one character at a time, when it changes. Use it for
    short text an agent rewrites while someone watches, such as a chat title.
    The first render shows the text at once.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><TypedTextDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Chat title"
      code={`import { TypedText } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/typed-text";

<h1 tabIndex={-1} title={chat.title} className="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-sm font-medium">
  <TypedText text={chat.title} animate={!chat.titleManual && chat.titleRevision > 1} />
</h1>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>text</code> is the full text. When it changes, the new text types in at
      25ms a character, and never takes longer than 800ms (<code
        >typedTextCharacterDuration</code
      > and
      <code>typedTextMaxDuration</code>). It steps by graphemes, so emoji and
      accented letters never split.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>animate</code> defaults to <code>true</code>. Pass
      <code>false</code> to show changes at once, such as a title someone typed by
      hand. The text is inline, so a truncating parent still adds an ellipsis. <code
        >className</code
      >, <code>data-*</code>, and other span attributes pass through.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Without animation</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Show changes at once"
      code={`<TypedText text="This sentence appears immediately." animate={false} />`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Screen readers get the full text at once from a visually hidden copy; the
      typing letters are hidden from them, so nothing is read in pieces. With
      reduced motion the text changes at once, and turning reduced motion on
      mid-change finishes it right away. While typing, the root has
      <code>data-state="typing"</code>; otherwise <code>"idle"</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Typed Text has no color or font of its own. It inherits from the heading
      or paragraph it sits in, in light, dark, and brand themes.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
